Subject: [PATCH] net: SOCKS5 username/password authentication (RFC 1929)

The SOCKS5 client supports RFC 1929 username and password
authentication, so the browser can connect through proxies that require
credentials. With credentials set, the greeting offers both no-auth and
username/password and the proxy picks. Without credentials, the greeting
is byte-identical to stock Chromium. Credentials stay out of
ProxyServer, so they never reach NetLog, net-export dumps or socket pool
keys.

